        "Across the edge-bundling and crowd-rendering sources, dense visual scenes become manageable by replacing raw geometric complexity with structured image-space or sample-based abstractions. Skeleton-based edge bundling clusters geometrically similar edges, inflates cluster shapes, extracts skeletons, and attracts edges toward locally centered targets; image-based crowd rendering similarly uses impostor samples, positional and directional discretization, and optimized texture storage to display large animated crowds at interactive rates.",
        "The shared concept is not merely acceleration: abstraction changes what the viewer can read. Edge bundling sacrifices individual edge identity and direction fidelity to expose coarse connectivity, while crowd impostors trade full per-avatar geometry for scalable visual presence. Shader raymarching provides a related but weaker cross-source bridge because it also treats geometry through mathematical spatial descriptions, marching rays through distance fields inside a fragment shader."
      ],
      "claim_ids": [
        "claim-skeletons-of-inflated-edge-cluster-shapes-provide-locally-centered-targets-for-b--27f82ed32127",
        "claim-hierarchical-agglomerative-clustering-with-full-linkage-and-euclidean-distances--759b1a2656e8",
